From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: support XP's Display Properties: theme previews and SetSystemVisualStyle

Purpose: let XP's Display Properties (themeui.dll) preview and apply visual
styles: Luna in its colours, other .msstyles files, and Windows Classic.
XP behavior: themeui opens classes of a theme file that is not active yet
(OpenThemeDataFromFile), draws its samples with DrawNCPreview and applies
the choice with SetSystemVisualStyle. Before applying a style it reads the
style's colours, sizes and fonts with GetThemeSysColor, GetThemeSysSize and
GetThemeSysFont on such a class, and sets them with SetSysColors and
SPI_SETNONCLIENTMETRICS after the style.
Wine before: the first two were unimplemented stubs, which abort the
program, and ordinal 65 did not exist. The GetThemeSys* functions looked
the metric up in the active theme whatever the handle: from the classic
look they returned the classic colours and sizes, which themeui then set
over the style's (Windows XP style kept the grey windows, the classic
selection and the classic caption).
Change: open a class from any opened theme file (its classes are read
without touching the system metrics); SetSystemVisualStyle opens and
applies the file, or the classic look without one; DrawNCPreview draws an
inactive window, an active window and a message box with the style's WINDOW
and BUTTON classes, or classic frames; GetThemeParseErrorInfo reports no
details instead of aborting; GetThemeSysBool, GetThemeSysColor,
GetThemeSysFont, GetThemeSysInt, GetThemeSysSize and GetThemeSysString read
the metrics of the theme file the class belongs to.
Scope: every Wine application (these were stubs or missing; the metrics of
a class of the active theme are the active theme's, as before).
---
